# Only the essential project files/folders are tracked — everything else at
# the repo root is ignored by default. The repo has accumulated a lot of
# one-off diagnostic/analysis scripts, large audit CSVs, and generated
# artifacts (checkpoints, logs, results, data, plots) over the course of
# this project; none of that belongs in the tracked history going forward.
/*

# --- Core package + entry points ---
!/divroute_fl/
!/baselines/
!/scripts/
!/run_pretrained_companion_experiments.py

# --- Documentation ---
!/README.md
!/DIVROUTE_ACCURACY_MASTER_PLAN.md
!/DIVROUTE_ALGORITHMS_MASTER_DOC.md
!/DIVROUTE_PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md
!/DIVROUTE_REMAINING_WORK.md

# --- Repo config ---
!/.gitignore

# --- Even inside allowed folders above, never track these ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/divroute_fl/main_diag4_polarityfixed.py

# --- Large-file safety net ---
# .gitignore can only match by name/pattern, not by size, so this only
# catches large files of these KNOWN types (model weights, archives,
# datasets) if one ever ends up inside an allowed folder above. It is not
# a substitute for the pre-commit size hook (see scripts/git-hooks/), which
# is the only thing that actually rejects a commit for being too big
# regardless of file type.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.h5
*.pkl
*.npy
*.npz
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
*.rar
